  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Education obligated $2.2B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department recorded 703 awards with an average award size of $3.1M. The Department's obligations were down 11.8% year over year. The fiscal-year series shows obligations of $2.7B in FY21, $2.4B in FY22, $2.4B in FY23, $2.7B in FY24, $2.5B in FY25, and $2.2B in FY26. The FY2026 totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. The largest NAICS category in the period is Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $930M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $670M. The top vendors in the period include ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $341M, NELNET SERVICING LLC at $294M, and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $245M. This snapshot highlights where the Department is spending to date and which firms and categories account for the biggest shares of contractual obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Education's contract spending changed over recent years?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations were $2.7B in FY21, $2.4B in FY22, $2.4B in FY23, $2.7B in FY24, $2.5B in FY25, and $2.2B in FY26. The Department of Education obligated $2.2B in FY2026 to date. The Department's obligations were down 11.8% year over year. The FY2026 totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which contract categories and vendors account for the largest shares?",
        "body": "Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation is the largest category at $930M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $670M. Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities totaled $148M, and Other Computer Related Services totaled $93M. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC is the largest vendor at $341M, followed by NELNET SERVICING LLC at $294M and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $245M."
      }
    ]
  },
